<title>FINLAND: Kyro shows muscle in bourse debut.</title>
<headline>Kyro shows muscle in bourse debut.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newly-listed shares in machinery and power group Kyro Oy began trading on Monday at 39.00 markka, 44 percent above the offering price of 27.00 markka, and brokers said the higher levels looked firm.</p>
<p>At 1225/0925 GMT, Kyro traded at 39.00 markka after touching 42.00 markka earlier in the session. Volume in the small cap was a hefty 21 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we'll see the share trading at around 39.00. There are buyers at these levels,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
